                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1d3eb3c-4bf3-389f-af80-53f9fe26baa9",
                        "entry_id": "f86f7d64-f72e-3f17-95bf-e81368d0eebf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ихтиол., рыбол., кулин. тонкая, но прочная плёнка, образующая мешок-оболочку, в котором находится икра лососёвых, осетровых и частиковых рыб"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e49b459-41d7-49d6-a391-7c53ce7bcd98",
                                "sense_id": "c1d3eb3c-4bf3-389f-af80-53f9fe26baa9",
                                "text": "Женщины освобождали икру от плёнки — ястыка, заполняли ею баки, пересыпая солью."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "994ee781-d5c6-48cf-a1eb-0f25b72b3e75",
                                "sense_id": "c1d3eb3c-4bf3-389f-af80-53f9fe26baa9",
                                "text": "В действительности отец Третьей был чёрной кости — он владел рыбной лавкой на окраине Хабаровска и славился тем, что, подбросив сазана, мог на лету вспороть ему брюхо и достать икру, не повредив ястыка."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "095b7cd2-df39-3ec6-83ac-13688175bcf0",
                        "entry_id": "f86f7d64-f72e-3f17-95bf-e81368d0eebf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ихтиол., рыбол., кулин. икра в такой плёнке"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0a9ea97-8f42-487d-b9e6-f9b443119a5e",
                                "sense_id": "095b7cd2-df39-3ec6-83ac-13688175bcf0",
                                "text": "Мишка выбирал самок и бросал отцу, а тот, зажав сигарету в углу рта и наклонив голову набок, вспарывал тонкое серебряное брюхо. Нежные фиолетово-мясные икряные ястыки бросал в таз, рыбу в воду."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "79c003a2-5599-4caf-97be-6ec8e5d80231",
                        "source_entry_id": "f86f7d64-f72e-3f17-95bf-e81368d0eebf",
                        "source_sense_description": "плёнка, образующая мешок-оболочку, в котором находится рыбная икра",
                        "target_lang_word": "skein",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "skein",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quantity of yarn, thread, etc. put up together in an oblong shape, after it is taken from the reel. A skein of cotton yarn is formed by eighty turns of the thread around a fifty-four inch reel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52f9a496-fb19-4d2d-88bb-92917c9fba66",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "Brau'd in mine owne houſe with a skeine of thred: / Away thou Ragge, thou quantitie, thou remnant,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d6e82a0-1806-4bde-a317-12b0c815520b",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "No? why art thou then exaſperate, thou idle, / immateriall skiene of Sleyd ſilke; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a54ffc00-97ab-4c8b-a6cd-85ec48c4390c",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "“How horribly unjust of you!” cried Lord Henry, tilting his hat back and looking up at the little clouds that, like ravelled skeins of glossy white silk, were drifting across the hollowed turquoise of the summer sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f38d8c8d-8535-4dd7-9278-711a1b883d5c",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "The embroidery, which was a matter for thought, the design being difficult and the colours wanting consideration, brought lapses into the dialogue when she seemed to be engrossed in her skeins of silk, or, with head a little drawn back and eyes narrowed, considered the effect of the whole."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bd17d27-21e0-4576-87da-3ec4404b4a3c",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "“He did have a beard, sir,” replied Dorcas, smiling. “And well I know it, for he borrowed two skeins of my black wool to make it with! And I’m sure it looked wonderfully natural at a distance.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d79b84f9-e2d3-448b-848b-003c244a0cfa",
                                                "sense_id": "71189785-f4a7-337f-9707-7d13ba34e752",
                                                "text": "You hold the skein: wind, Thomas, wind / The thread of eternal life and death."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A web, a weave, a tangle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0dfd0f9-868e-427c-95a7-c1fd9b924d30",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "He watched her pretty and unconscious munching through the skeins of smoke that pervaded the tent[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2dc1b52-3d62-406e-9f09-cd73843a9355",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "But when she turned her thoughts to Morningside Park she perceived the tangled skein of life was now to be further complicated by his romantic importunity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0681924c-0291-49fb-9df1-5881fa46fe27",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "The practical application of what I have said is very close to the problem which I am investigating. It is a tangled skein, you understand, and I am looking for a loose end."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2403de7-5b26-4fa0-9151-9196b061e8fa",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "But then, science is a complex skein, intricately interknotted across the artificial boundaries we draw only that we may the more easily encompass its parts in our mind. Pick up any thread of that skein and the whole structure will follow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac68546c-5b6e-4f9d-ab62-fc448ff15329",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "Then, beginning in 1959, the skein of convention began to unravel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e85beaa-a441-4d46-909e-ed306cd6c155",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "Ted began to walk, still dazed, until he found himself among a skein of backstreets so narrow they felt dark."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f40820b8-9835-4b70-b3e4-148540f2d62c",
                                                "sense_id": "fca47707-ba57-35dd-92a3-ef0791256e62",
                                                "text": "It was the latest in a skein of legal maneuvers by the prince’s lawyers to defuse Ms. Giuffre’s case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48190d46-53a2-3305-8bc4-1f5e274cfd8d",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The membrane of a fish ovary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23c59be5-9a15-35cd-bd9c-a3db0d8601b5",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metallic strengthening band or thimble on the wooden arm of an axle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7678637b-e60b-4890-aeb1-19c172d6c48d",
                                                "sense_id": "23c59be5-9a15-35cd-bd9c-a3db0d8601b5",
                                                "text": "One of the free-state settlers went to the blacksmith's shop unarmed, carrying a waggon skein to be repaired."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32136115-a93d-39fd-827a-c245013f05bf",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of wild fowl (e.g. geese, goslings) when they are in flight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "collective",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "891c83ce-130f-416c-8f5d-20160772aedb",
                                                "sense_id": "32136115-a93d-39fd-827a-c245013f05bf",
                                                "text": "High above the swallows and 2 miles or so out into the Channel was a skein of geese, probably brent geese on the first day of their emigration from the estuaries of the Channel coast towards the high Arctic tundra of Spitsbergen or Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a0fb79a-3ca0-4dde-80d4-747ad0cde0d6",
                                                "sense_id": "32136115-a93d-39fd-827a-c245013f05bf",
                                                "text": "They're only referred to as a gaggle when they're on land. When they're flying in formation they can be referred to as a skein."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9efbf69f-c56b-32e6-ba92-ddc75596f214",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A winning streak."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf807767-8ca9-306e-b6fd-2620478b1ba5",
                                        "entry_id": "102149ec-46c1-3fd6-835f-9d1be7d0ad73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A series created by a web (major broadcasting network)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a49e51b-c51d-439a-acf6-e1f221c5ee71",
                                                "sense_id": "bf807767-8ca9-306e-b6fd-2620478b1ba5",
                                                "text": "All three tele skeins are pitching furiously to snag the super Easter Day tele show to be bankrolled by Frigidaire, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29c14625-a24d-479b-bf85-e21b069b1b8b",
                                                "sense_id": "bf807767-8ca9-306e-b6fd-2620478b1ba5",
                                                "text": "Three comedy shows from the U. S. are in the CTV lineup: CBSTV's Phil Silvers and Danny Thomas skeins and NBC-TV's \"Harry's Girls.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "skein",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37ea88d6-deb1-3f65-a88e-bcdbd35dd87c",
                                        "entry_id": "e5448f60-631d-3b43-8b2e-a0b666327565",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To wind or weave into a skein."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
